drm: fall back to the gbm platform when no EGL device matches

Against aquamarine 0.15.0 (tag v0.15.0), the version Arch ships beside
Hyprland 0.56.2. Not submitted upstream.

`CDRMRenderer::attempt` builds a renderer only through `EGL_PLATFORM_DEVICE_EXT`,
matching an EGL device against the DRM node it was handed. `vmlord_drm` is
KMS-only -- `DRIVER_GEM | DRIVER_MODESET | DRIVER_ATOMIC`, no `DRIVER_RENDER` --
so there is no render node, and `/dev/dxg` is not a DRM device at all. Mesa
therefore enumerates exactly one EGL device, the software one, and it carries no
DRM file to match on: both `eglQueryDeviceStringEXT` calls answer
`EGL_BAD_PARAMETER`. No renderer is built, `initMgpu` fails, and the output is
modeset and never painted -- `hyprctl monitors` reports `Virtual-2 0x0@60`, and
the log says `Can't create renderer, no matching devices found`.

Mutter is untouched by this because it takes `EGL_PLATFORM_GBM_KHR` on the card's
own fd, where Mesa loads the kms-dri screen; so does Hyprland's own renderer,
which is why the compositor runs and serves clients while showing nothing. That
is also the second `CDRMRenderer::attempt` overload, which aquamarine has written
and never calls -- no caller of it exists anywhere in the tree.

So call it when the first returns nothing, at both sites, each of which already
holds the GBM allocator it needs a line above. A device that does match an EGL
device never reaches the fallback, so nothing changes for a guest with a real GPU.

Measured on this guest: before, the output stayed at 0x0 and nothing was drawn;
after, the desktop comes up at 1920x1080 -- on llvmpipe with the distribution's
Mesa, and on the host's adapter with the payload's, once the dma-buf halves of
`0001-d3d12-scan-out-through-a-winsys-displaytarget.patch` are there to carry the
buffer.

Nothing in this repository builds aquamarine, so nothing applies this yet. See
the README beside it.

Refs: #200
